  "explanation": {
    "en": "何 (なに／なん) means “what.” It is used to ask about things, actions, or information. The reading changes depending on the following sound.\n\nKey points:\n• 何 (なに) is common before particles: 何を, 何で\n• 何 (なん) is common before です/だ or counters: 何ですか, 何人\n• Use it to ask about objects, activities, or details\n• Often appears with particles like を, が, で\n\nExample: “これは何ですか” means “What is this?” “何を食べますか” means “What will you eat?”\n\nThe reading “なん” is used before です and many counters: 何ですか, 何人 (なんにん). For other cases, “なに” is safer.\n\nPractice by asking simple questions: 何をしますか, 何が好きですか, 何で行きますか.",
    "ja": ""
  },
